A||||2||Fiero86||Can a Fiero SE be a sport coupe.?||||1||
Z||000000||Fiero86||08-09-2000||08:14 PM||||I have a 1986 Fiero Sport Coupe. IS that a version of an SE, or is it different? Someone please explain.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||08-10-2000||01:57 AM||||An SC (sports coupe) is a base model with a few options.  The SE looks like an '85 GT without the GT badges, usually with the 2.8.  One is not the other.  The SC does <B>not</B> have the aero fascias or the ground fx.  The SE does.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||08-10-2000||02:01 AM||||The 84 SE the same as the 85 thru 88 sport Coupe. (more options than the base coupe.<BR>The 85 SE had the V-6 as an option but the coupe body style. 85 Sport Coupe had 13" aluminum wheels (finned) as standard and the 14" were optional.<BR>86 and 87 SE had the same "aero" package as the 85 GT.<BR>There are no 88 SE's The SE was dropped in favor of the Formula.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 08-10-2000).]||||reg||1
